---
export const title = 'Navigation';
export const order = 300;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  By default (<code>navigation="none"</code>) the steps are not buttons. To let the person move
  between steps:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>navigation="linear"</code>: steps up to the first unfinished required step are buttons, so
    the person can go back to any earlier step but not skip ahead. Optional and disabled steps do
    not block, and an earlier step with <code>error</code> does.
  </li>
  <li><code>navigation="free"</code>: every step that is not disabled is a button.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Activating a step fires <code>change</code> with <code>detail.value</code> and
  <code>detail.index</code>, then moves <code>current</code>. The event is cancelable: call
  <code>preventDefault()</code> to keep the current step, for example while the current step's form
  is invalid.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%;'>
    <wc-stepper id='stepper-linear' navigation='linear' current='shipping' label='Checkout'>
      <wc-step value='cart' label='Cart'></wc-step>
      <wc-step value='shipping' label='Shipping'></wc-step>
      <wc-step value='payment' label='Payment'></wc-step>
      <wc-step value='review' label='Review'></wc-step>
    </wc-stepper>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#stepper-linear').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change: ' + event.detail.value + ' (' + event.detail.index + ')');
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%;'>
    <wc-stepper navigation='free' current='profile' label='Settings'>
      <wc-step value='profile' label='Profile'></wc-step>
      <wc-step value='security' label='Security'></wc-step>
      <wc-step value='billing' label='Billing' disabled></wc-step>
      <wc-step value='notifications' label='Notifications'></wc-step>
    </wc-stepper>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>
